  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preparing Sevi for more impact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sevi is a software company based in the Netherlands and Kenya. Sevi provides software to (African) funds and banks to serve a traditionally difficult target group: small business owners. DGGF has provided them with a startup loan of EUR 400k in 2023 (DGGF2303).
SEVI is the only B2B stock lending app that is fully tailored to the order cycles and order volumes of the informal microentrepreneurs. That means that SEVI finances stock orders from as low as $10 up to $3k at a flexible loan tenure of 1 to 90 days. SEVI does so at a 3 to 8x lower weekly rate as compared to its competitors
Sevi experiences a rapid growth in Kenya. Since market introduction, Sevi has created a solid customer base of 2,500 informal micro-entrepreneurs and the monthly lending volumes that are issued to these micro-entrepreneurs have witnessed an average 25% monthly increase.
Over 27 million Kenyans live in informal settlements of which 4 million in slums. So 27 million Kenyans buy their groceries (e.g. flour, cooking oil, milk products, toiletries, and pain relievers) from around 250,000 dukas (home-based micro retail-outlets, kiosks) that are spread across the slums and informal neighborhoods. Unlike formal retail formulas (that sell large units), dukas allow customers to purchase what they can afford (i.e. what they have at hand) by offering products in small volumes that meet their daily need.</narrative>
  </description>
